  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word commonly used in business, government, and medical contexts. The {軽減|けいげん}{税率|ぜいりつ} (reduced tax rate) became a major topic in Japan when the consumption tax was raised to 10% in 2019, with certain items like food kept at 8%.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {負担|ふたん}{軽減|けいげん} (burden reduction)\n- {軽減|けいげん}{税率|ぜいりつ} (reduced tax rate)\n- {痛|いた}みの{軽減|けいげん} (pain alleviation)\n- {軽減|けいげん}{措置|そち} (relief measures)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {削減|さくげん}: reduction — focuses on cutting back amounts or costs\n- {緩和|かんわ}: easing, relaxation — used for regulations, tensions, or symptoms",
